/*  EXPECTED: COMPILES and runs; compiled output must match the interpreter.

    Legal captures — none of these escape a region, so the outward-only invariant
    has nothing to refuse. Each closure captures an enclosing binding and WRITES to it.

    ★ Captures are BY VALUE in both backends, so a write through a capture updates the
    closure's OWN copy and the enclosing binding is unchanged. Every line below therefore
    prints 0, not the written value. Write-back through a capture is not a language
    feature, and this file pins that down.

    This file is also the regression case for the capture-completeness bug: a body that
    only WRITES a captured variable (never reads it) used to leave the variable
    uncaptured, emitting an undeclared C variable. */

Bind number to run-size, given (the series of number s):
    Define count as 0.
    Bind void to measure, given ():
        count becomes the number of s.
    Done.
    Cast measure on ().
    return count.
Done.

Bind void to run-value, given (the number n):
    Define tally as 0.
    Bind void to add-n, given ():
        tally becomes tally + n.
    Done.
    Cast add-n on ().
    State "Write through a value capture (enclosing unchanged, expect 0): {tally}".
Done.

Bind void to run-local, given ():
    Define store as a series of number.
    Define fresh as a series of number with (7, 8, 9).
    Bind void to fill, given ():
        store becomes fresh.
    Done.
    Cast fill on ().
    State "Write through a region capture (enclosing unchanged, expect 0): {the number of store}".
Done.

Pull a rabbit.
    Define inner as a series of number with (1, 2, 3).
    Define n as Cast run-size on (inner).
    State "Write to a captured local from a closure (enclosing unchanged, expect 0): {n}".
Done.
Cast run-value on (42).
Cast run-local on ().
